{"content":[{"c":["BEEROTH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["One of four Hivite cities that secured Joshua’s promise not to destroy them when the Israelites marched into Canaan (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.9.17","r":"Josh.9.17","rawR":"Josh.9.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.9.17","value":"Josh.9.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 9:17"},"). Beeroth was later identified as a city in Benjamin’s territory (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.18.25","r":"Josh.18.25","rawR":"Josh.18.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.18.25","value":"Josh.18.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 18:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.4.2-3","r":"2Sam.4.2-3","rawR":"2Sam.4.2-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.4.2-3","value":"2Sam.4.2-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 4:2-3"},"). It was the home of Rechab and Baanah, assassins of King Ishbosheth (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.4.2-9","r":"2Sam.4.2-9","rawR":"2Sam.4.2-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.4.2-9","value":"2Sam.4.2-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 4:2-9"},"), and of Naharai, Joab’s armor bearer (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.37","r":"2Sam.23.37","rawR":"2Sam.23.37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.37","value":"2Sam.23.37"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:37"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.39","r":"1Chr.11.39","rawR":"1Chr.11.39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.39","value":"1Chr.11.39"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:39"},"). The city was repopulated after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.25","r":"Ezra.2.25","rawR":"Ezra.2.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.25","value":"Ezra.2.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.29","r":"Neh.7.29","rawR":"Neh.7.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.29","value":"Neh.7.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:29"},"). El Bireh near Ramallah and Nebi Samwil north of Jerusalem have both been suggested as possible locations for Beeroth."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Beeroth","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 9:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.9.17","rawQueryValue":"Josh.9.17","sourceRefExact":"Josh.9.17"},{"anchorText":"Jos 18:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.18.25","rawQueryValue":"Josh.18.25","sourceRefExact":"Josh.18.25"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 4:2-3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.4.2-3","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.4.2-3","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.4.2-3"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 4:2-9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.4.2-9","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.4.2-9","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.4.2-9"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 23:37","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.23.37","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.23.37","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.23.37"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 11:39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.11.39","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.11.39","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.11.39"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 2:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.2.25","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.2.25","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.2.25"},{"anchorText":"Neh 7:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.7.29","rawQueryValue":"Neh.7.29","sourceRefExact":"Neh.7.29"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"f5f621727e805ba9b2b21f47663f24367a203916fca56472bf161dfa04ef3384","sourceItemName":"Beeroth","sourceItemOrder":145,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Beeroth","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Beeroth","title":"Beeroth","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}